@startuml
title BERA - Generic Provider Search Sequence (Implementation PR A)

actor User
participant TrackerState
participant SearchIntent
participant AcquisitionBudgetPolicy as Policy
participant BoundedAcquisitionPlan as Plan
participant "execute_bounded_provider_search()" as LogicalSearch
participant "Existing Provider Operation" as ProviderOperation
participant "Provider Adapter / Port" as Provider
participant ProviderRunMetrics as Metrics
participant ProviderRunResult as Result
participant SearchSessionSnapshot as Snapshot

User -> TrackerState : Search(query, display_limit, providers)
TrackerState -> TrackerState : increment generation
TrackerState -> SearchIntent : create generation-bound intent
TrackerState -> Policy : validate display_limit
Policy --> TrackerState : valid bounded display limit
TrackerState -> Policy : create_plan / validate_plan
Policy -> Plan : approved finite budget + max acquisitions
Plan --> TrackerState : policy-backed plan
TrackerState -> LogicalSearch : execute(intent, approved plan, policy)

loop bounded internal acquisitions
  LogicalSearch -> ProviderOperation : execute(step)
  ProviderOperation -> Provider : existing bounded search(...)
  Provider --> ProviderOperation : provider response
  ProviderOperation --> LogicalSearch : safe AcquisitionBatch
  LogicalSearch -> LogicalSearch : provider-integrity validation
  LogicalSearch -> LogicalSearch : stable-ID dedup only
  LogicalSearch -> LogicalSearch : aggregate candidates
  alt enough usable candidates AND safe early termination
    LogicalSearch -> LogicalSearch : stop when ordering/scope remain truthful
  else approved budget remains
    LogicalSearch -> LogicalSearch : continue next planned step
  end
end

LogicalSearch -> Metrics : build truthful aggregate metrics
note right of Metrics
  acquisition_budget != acquisition_requested
  Example: budget = 30
  two executed steps of 5
  requested = 10
end note

LogicalSearch -> Result : create generation-bound ProviderRunResult
note right of Result
  Result contains:
  generation copied from SearchIntent
  SUCCESS / EMPTY / ERROR
  COMPLETE / PARTIAL / unavailable
  ordered usable pool
  frozen canonical prefix
end note
LogicalSearch -> LogicalSearch : canonical_session_results = ordered_usable_pool[0:display_limit]
LogicalSearch --> TrackerState : ProviderRunResult
TrackerState -> Snapshot : commit(result)
alt result.generation == intent.generation
  Snapshot -> Snapshot : immutable provider commit
else stale result generation
  Snapshot -> Snapshot : ignore/reject stale result
end
Snapshot --> TrackerState : current frozen session state
TrackerState --> User : session state

note over TrackerState,LogicalSearch
  TrackerState coordinates only.
  It does not implement:
  budget policy, provider strategy, deduplication,
  or provider-specific geographic logic.
end note

note over LogicalSearch,ProviderOperation
  Multiple internal calls belong to ONE logical provider search.
  They are not orchestrator retries.
end note

note over ProviderOperation,Provider
  Existing low-level provider semantics remain unchanged.
  Facebook execute() -> one Actor run remains valid.
end note

note over Plan,Result
  Geographic source of truth in PR A:
  requested scope lives on SearchIntent / plan;
  effective scope and coverage_status are derived
  from the plan onto ProviderRunResult.
  AcquisitionBatch does not carry effective scope.
  Concrete Facebook Venezuela partitions are PR D.
end note
@enduml
